Use consistent mmap/unmap sizes in MemoryIntArray

Ensure mmap/munmap pairings for MemoryIntArray always use the same size
argument, rather than re-querying the ashmem size region before unmap.
This prevents any kind of changes to the underlying fd from bleeding
into the size argument used in the munmap call.

A longer term fix will migrate this class to be implemented purely in
terms of SharedMemory and existing Java primitives.

